 "correction_note": "v1 is WITHDRAWN. Two defects, both found in external review: (1) it screened the training population with an OSM oneway>=0.5 feature test (39 stations, 1514 rows) while the deployed dirsplit model screens on the OBSERVED share band [0.15, 0.85] (81 stations, 3665 rows), so v1 scored a different population than the deployment; and (2) it named its gradient-boosting entrant 'similarity_weighted_lgbm' and reported its -31.6% / -39.2% scores as if they were the DEPLOYED LightGBM's. They were not: the entrant is fit on this table, on these folds, with a similarity kernel aimed at the training centroid, while the deployment aims its kernel at the Gothenburg sensor edges and is evaluated on a held-out Gothenburg station. The claim 'the deployed LightGBM is 31.6-39.2% worse than 50/50' is WITHDRAWN as unsupported; nothing here measures the deployed model. The entrant is renamed lgbm_reimplementation and every candidate carries deployment_equivalent = false.",
